{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"git show 9e1116b:docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-String -Pattern 'BATCH SHAPE|two-row|MULTI-ROW' -Context 0,1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"git show 9e1116b:docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-String -Pattern 'BATCH SHAPE|two-row|MULTI-ROW' -Context 0,1\"","aggregated_output":"\r\n> method = \"\"\"The verdict record's two halves, each driven beside its opposite so neither reads as a rule with one \r\nanswer. THE IDENTITY, pure over synthetic `git ls-tree -r` entries: a listing and the same listing plus a round file, \r\na log fragment and a session log fold EQUAL, while a changed work blob and a changed docs/work/ spec each fold \r\nDIFFERENT - so the exclusion is proven to be an exclusion rather than a fold that ignores everything. THE ENCODING \r\nBOUNDARY, driven through git rather than asserted about it: a record path holding a non-ASCII character - the shape \r\ngit QUOTES, asserted in the fixture so it cannot silently stop reproducing - leaves the identity unmoved, while an \r\naccented WORK path moves it; and raw listings with one blob renamed from invalid-UTF-8 path byte 200 to 201 - asserted \r\nto COLLIDE under replacement decoding - fold DIFFERENT through tree_identity, so parsing and the ASCII record-prefix \r\nboundary occur before any decode. THE TRAILER GRAMMAR: format/parse round-trip; the LAST trailer in a message governs, \r\nso a rework commit quoting the round it answers does not have the quotation read as its own attestation; and three \r\nmalformed shapes - a verdict word outside the enum, a 40-hex tree, a missing round count - each fail to PARSE rather \r\nthan parse to something. THE NAME PARSE: a round file with and without the relaxed tag, the pre-train flat layout, a \r\nsession log, and the legacy hand-authored rollup answering None because it names no reviewed sha. THE GATE, on a \r\ntwo-branch git fixture with the trunk checked out: a logged reviewer round naming the current tree clears it with NO \r\nrollup present anywhere; the same file with a BUILD session log behind it does not (the implementer-authored round); a \r\nSECOND round file committed behind that ONE session log, whose NAME claims the other declared phase, is not a second \r\nreviewer - both files are asserted committed and the single log with them, the entries carry the LOG's phase, so at a \r\ndeclared policy of 2 REVIEW-B is still outstanding and the gate refuses by name until a REVIEW-B whose own session log \r\ndeclares it arrives and clears it; TWO session logs at ONE (train, ordinal) declaring DIFFERENT review phases - both \r\nasserted committed, with the round file they would otherwise phase asserted still present so the empty answer is the \r\nambiguity rule and not an empty scan - serve NO round at all rather than letting the last log read win, and the gate \r\nrefuses by name while the single-log arm beside it clears; a round whose tree was reworked away does not, while a \r\nlog-fragment and scoreboard commit after a round leaves it governing; a CHANGES-REQUESTED round refuses; and a \r\nverified Review-Verdict trailer contradicting the rounds refuses by name in its verdict word and in a round count \r\nABOVE the evidence, while a count BELOW it does NOT - both directions driven, because the writer is best-effort and a \r\nstamp the evidence outruns is a missed stamp whose refusal parked an approved lane at the very stop the cross-check \r\nexists to prevent - and TWO attestations at one governing tree leave the NEWEST governing so a legitimately re-drawn \r\nround is not accused of forgery. THE CARRIER IS VERIFIED AND NOT ONLY PARSED, which is what \"the trailer cannot create \r\nan approval\" costs: the identical attestation words on a commit that CHANGED the work under them - asserted in the \r\nfixture to have really moved the governing identity - are read at neither the tree they NAME nor the tree they rode, \r\nbeside the record-only carrier of the same words that IS read, so copying a true attestation onto later work buys \r\nnothing. THE WRITER IS DRIVEN END TO END, not only the trailer helper: a completed round is run through the loop's own \r\ncomplete_review_round on a repository fixture and the commit it lands is asserted to CARRY the attestation, to name \r\nthe governing tree, to be read back by the branch reader under the key the cross-check looks up, to leave that \r\ngoverning tree unmoved, and to satisfy the gate - the whole path between a round completing and its attestation \r\nlanding, which every other trailer case skipped by committing the string itself, and which nothing anywhere reports \r\nwhen it stops writing because absence is the state the cross-check must stand down on. THE RESUME'S OWED SET IS THE \r\nEVIDENCE'S ALONE: with both declared phases served at the governing tree and a stale untracked owed-marker still \r\npresent - the state a run killed between the last reviewer's commit and the round completing leaves - the resume is \r\nasserted to queue NOTHING, and beside it a genuine rework with one phase redrawn is asserted to queue that phase and \r\nonly it. THE PEEL: a genuine Bar-Green refresh commit, verified against its own tree and parent, moves the branch \r\ntip's identity and neither reader's answer - the loop still says no round is owed and the gate still merges - which is \r\nthe one commit class two separately-chosen revs disagreed on; and the same refresh with a coordinator TELEMETRY commit \r\nstacked on top of it - a record path, so the fold ignores it and only the tip-only peel could be defeated by it - \r\nstill owes no round and still merges. THE SECOND DISPOSABLE CLASS, the machinery's own MECHANICAL adjudication close \r\nadmitted by mechanical_close_attestation, is driven beside it in the same idiom - the positive and its subject/path \r\nrefusals - so the peel reads as a verified ADMISSION and not as a subject match. The positive: a mechanical close \r\nwritten through the composed close subject and touching only docs/work/ is asserted to REALLY have moved the branch's \r\ntree - without which the test would pass on a peel that had nothing to do - and the round it follows still governs and \r\nstill merges, with no legacy rollup present anywhere; without that peel the close archiving a judged row stales the \r\nAPPROVE that had just judged it, which is the failure this arm exists for and the one an adjudication lane cannot \r\navoid by ordering, since its round is drawn while the row is still in active/. The two peels are then driven \r\nCOMPOSING, a station refresh stacked on the close, because a lane produces them in that order. The refusals, and every \r\none of them is driven with the OTHER clauses satisfied, so each is the single thing that turns its commit away. A \r\nclose carrying a HAND-WRITTEN subject is an ordinary work commit and does not peel; a commit with the PUBLIC \r\nmechanical prefix/suffix but a FORGED middle is refused because the attestor derives the actual active/ -> complete/ \r\nWI ids from the no-renames git diff and re-composes their exact canonical subject; a close carrying the machinery's \r\nown subject that also touched a path OUTSIDE docs/work/ does not peel either; and INSIDE docs/work/ is not enough, \r\nbecause only the move itself may create or destroy - a close that SMUGGLED a brand-new spec in beside the move, and a \r\nclose that DESTROYED an already-terminal archived record beside it, are each refused, since peeling either would \r\nmeasure a spec's injection or a judged row's deletion at the parent where no reviewer ever saw it. A close whose pairs \r\ncame out of a SECOND lane's active/ directory is refused by the one-source-branch requirement, driven with everything \r\nelse valid - paths confined, deletions paired with their own additions, the subject exactly the one the writer \r\ncomposes for those ids - so nothing but that clause can be answering. THE MULTI-ROW SHAPE is driven too: a mechanical \r\nclose moving two rows does not peel, failing toward more review. All the refusal arms are asserted to leave the gate \r\nrefusing BY NAME on the round no longer naming the current tree, which is the fail-toward-MORE-review direction every \r\nunverified identity-moving step here takes. THE WRITER IS DRIVEN AGAINST THE VERIFIER, not only against fixtures the \r\ntest file composes itself: a REAL close is landed through handback.close_adjudication and the commit it produces is \r\nasserted to peel back to exactly the rev the lane was on, so an ordering or a spelling that drifted on either side is \r\na red rather than a silently un-peelable close on every adjudication lane. THE EMPTY CLOSE is driven where it is \r\nOBSERVABLE and its consequence is stated rather than assumed to match the others: a commit carrying the composed \r\nsubject and a single parent that changed NOTHING - a real --allow-empty commit, since a zero-path diff is the one \r\nclose shape a fixture cannot reach by writing files - is asserted refused AT mechanical_close_attestation, and \r\ndeliberately NOT asserted at the gate, because measurement says the gate cannot see this refusal at all. Its refusal \r\nis OVER-DETERMINED and no clause owns it, which is stated rather than glossed: the one-source-branch requirement turns \r\nit away first, and with THAT deleted the empty diff derives no ids at all, whose composed subject (`adjudicate:  -> \r\ncomplete/ (mechanical close)`) cannot equal the one the commit carries - so the exact-subject comparison refuses it \r\nregardless, and there is deliberately no third non-emptiness clause, which could only ever fire where these two \r\nalready had. The consequence is asserted beside the refusal because they are the honest pair: an empty commit \r\npreserves the identity by construction, so governing_rev's walk-through step reaches the real close underneath either \r\nway, and a test asserting a gate refusal here would be asserting a behaviour the module does not have and should not, \r\nsince a commit that changed nothing has invalidated no verdict. THE TWO PEELS' REFUSAL ARMS are held by \r\ntests/test_integrate_station.py, cited beside this module because integrate re-exports these very functions \r\n(refresh_attestation, work_tip) and the station suite is where a refresh can be produced rather than hand-written: a \r\ngenuine refresh attested to the sha it produced; a forged Bar-Green trailer in three shapes, the sharpest being a \r\ngenuine refresh message copied verbatim onto another commit; an amend that keeps the message while the tree moves, \r\nrevoking the attestation; the deliberately forged attestation recorded as a STATED limit rather than a defence; and \r\nthe reset peel's data-loss half - an honest work commit merely QUOTING the trailer is never peeled away, and a genuine \r\nrefresh above it peels back to exactly that commit. BOTH carriers are driven, not only the convenient one: that \r\nnon-empty telemetry commit, and then the EMPTY commit agent_common.commit_telemetry writes when a Review-Verdict \r\nattestation must land on unchanged bookkeeping - obtained by CALLING that producer rather than by hand, so the two \r\ncannot drift apart, and asserted to really be zero-path, because that is the commit shape a walk classifying PATHS \r\ncould not classify and so stopped at, burying the refresh under the very commit that recorded the approval. A WORK \r\ncommit above the refresh does re-owe and does refuse, so the walk is proven to step through what cannot invalidate a \r\nverdict rather than through everything. BOTH ORDERS of refresh and round, because only one of them was covered and the \r\nother was broken: the round drawn AFTER the refresh - the order the shipped path actually produces, since a lane's \r\nrefresh is spawned as soon as its worker is DONE and before the merge slot runs, so any slot refusal parks a branch \r\nwith a refresh and no round - cites the POST-refresh sha, asserted in the fixture to be that sha and not the \r\npre-refresh one, and is asserted to serve the lane at both readers and to carry the coordinator's attestation under \r\nthe key the cross-check looks it up by, while a rework above it still re-owes. THE ATTESTATION'S CARRIER IS SCOPED TO \r\nITS OWN PATHS, on BOTH arms and not only the one that carries a pathspec: with an unrelated work file staged and the \r\nbookkeeping unchanged, the commit agent_common.commit_telemetry writes for NAMED paths and the one it writes for NO \r\npaths at all - the call this suite itself makes, and the arm where a scope appended only when paths exist evaporates - \r\nare each asserted zero-path with the caller's index left exactly as found, so work cannot land under a bookkeeping \r\nlabel nor an attestation ride a commit that changed the tree. THE DIAL: the three values over a brief-and-drafts \r\nmatrix, an unrecognized value falling to when-minting rather than to never, and an adjudication lane closing with a \r\nsuccessor draft merging with no verdict artifact of any kind under both never and when-minting, while a spine draft \r\nstill owes its round. THE DIAL AT THE SCHEDULER, the half a reader could otherwise only take on trust: a committing \r\nADJUDICATE session is driven through the loop's own bookkeeping arm on a closed-lane repository at every dial value - \r\nincluding the `always` no repository fixture had reached - and the review queue it leaves is asserted together with \r\nthe train-scoped diff range and the recorded judging family, which is what \"exactly as a committing BUILD does\" has to \r\nmean. Its INPUT is driven beside it: a branch carrying its spec in BOTH homes, the terminal copy drafting a spine \r\nsuccessor and a stale active copy an ordinary one, is asserted to answer the scheduler and the merge gate the SAME \r\nway, with the shared precedence also driven pure on a two-path list and on the empty one. THE SHARED DEFINITION, in \r\nBOTH its dimensions. WHICH TREE: the C2 review-owed derivation answers owed after a rework and served after a fresh \r\nround, and record-only commits after the verdict re-owe nothing. HOW MANY PHASES: at a declared policy of 2 a lone \r\nlogged REVIEW-A APPROVE is REFUSED by name and the gate clears only once a governing REVIEW-B joins it at the same \r\nidentity; and the half-drawn round a killed run leaves - REVIEW-A served, the in-memory phase queue gone - is answered \r\nby both readers together, the derivation naming REVIEW-B and ONLY REVIEW-B while the gate refuses, then both agreeing \r\nonce it lands, with the same fixture asserted SERVED at policy 1 so the answer is proven to come from the declared \r\ncount. The phase span is driven pure at the values neither caller reaches - a negative policy, which a bare slice \r\nwould answer by slicing from the END, and an over-dialled one - and an unparseable or refusable round is owed on both \r\nsides: it is drawn again and never clears the gate. The one class the readers still disagree on is a dissent: it is \r\nserved for `phases_owed` and refused by the gate. THE TIER IS THE WHOLE CITED SET'S, not the majority's: the cited set \r\nincludes slow modules, including test_integrate_admission, test_integrate_station, test_handback, test_bar_attestation \r\nand test_verdict_record, so Full is the cheapest tier at which EVERY arm above actually runs and Smoke would have \r\nclaimed commit-floor coverage for a set the commit floor only partly runs. Tier and the pytest marker remain \r\nindependent declarations that no check compares (registry-machinery-reference §12.2); this cell is labelled on the \r\nside that under-claims. THE GATING-SCOPE AND FILING BOUNDARY: a coordinator-recorded final claim-base round clears \r\nonly with persisted-final-reviewer mode and reviewer retention on; retained-session full rounds and narrow rounds \r\nhold; a missing claim base holds by name; the full claim-base range survives a trunk refresh while a partial range \r\ncannot gate; a partial or refusable latest round holds without falling back to an older APPROVE and is owed again; \r\nneither a narrow approve nor an invalid round suppresses the unchanged-rework page; and a legacy rollup never clears. \r\nTHE BAR ATTESTATION: a trailer validates only when its column-0 single label has its own tree and first parent, a \r\nknown bar, and a tests digest; wrong tree or parent, missing or unknown bar, missing tests, a quoted or duplicate \r\nlabel refuse. Digesting normalizes and de-duplicates named paths, is order-independent, differs for a changed set, and \r\ngives none for an empty set. A verified review attestation is never recognized as a refresh by work_tip or \r\ngoverning_rev, while the read-only walk still steps through an identity-preserving review carrier; verified landing \r\nand no-bar refresh attestations still peel. The refresh writes landing or no-bar through the shared producer, and \r\nrefresh and attest both reach that producer.\"\"\"\r\n  tier = \"Full\"\r\n> method = \"\"\"A registry row id as a declared input, three ways. THE DECLARATION: observation_tc_findings and \r\ninput_escape called on an in-memory observation case whose inputs name a registry row by id (SR-184, LLR-233, TC-055, \r\nSN-043, DA-001), alone and beside a repository path: the id is not an escaping path and the case raises no failure and \r\nno advisory. THE SUPPORT PATHS: the re-judge checkpoint's support paths for an id are the registry directories and \r\nnever a file named after the id, while a path input is its own support path. THE DIGEST: over a two-row requirement \r\nregistry under a temporary directory, the writer's inputs digest of SR-184 differs from that of an id no row carries, \r\nstays unchanged when only the other row is edited, and changes when only SR-184 is edited.\"\"\"\r\n  tier = \"Smoke\"\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
